================================================================================
Search cache for the Original Graph: asserted companions + asserted routing
================================================================================

Context:
The search cache had one set of adjacency and property companions, built from
the certified (effective) graph. The Original Graph (asserted relation) only had
its own entity-search table. Two defects followed:
1. Delta: the asserted view name (`…_asserted`) was not recognised as an
   asserted relation, so Original Graph Preview seeds came from the union
   entity search (derived triples included), and Original Graph expansion walked
   the certified `_adj_*` / `_props` tables built with derived triples.
2. Lakebase: the same asserted-name gap sent Preview to the union entity search;
   the Original Graph had no adjacency or props companion, so every expansion
   fell back to SPO (correct, but slow).
Fix: a second family of companions built from the asserted relation, routed by
name. The Original Graph now reads only asserted companions, so it can use the
cache without derived triples. The certified family is unchanged.

Changes:
1. src/back/core/graphdb/entity_search.py: `is_asserted_only_relation` also
   returns True for a `…_asserted` leaf (the asserted view on both backends).
2. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/_table_naming.py: new FQNs and suffixes
   `_asserted_adj_out`, `_asserted_adj_in`, `_asserted_props`; added to
   `graph_leaf_suffixes()` so Settings grouping (`object_base`) folds them into
   their domain.
3. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/ReadStore.py: `adjacency_table_ids` and
   `props_table_id` route by relation (asserted names for asserted relations),
   with and without a bound domain.
4. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/MaterializedStore.py: `rebuild_adjacency` builds
   the asserted adjacency and props from the asserted relation; one worker per
   companion (8 jobs) instead of min(5, N).
5. src/back/core/graphdb/lakebase/_adjacency_ddl.py: `asserted_adj_out_phy`,
   `asserted_adj_in_phy`, `asserted_props_phy` (`<base>_asserted_*`).
6. src/back/core/graphdb/lakebase/FlatStore.py: routing by relation; the
   rebuild moved out to `_companion_rebuild.py` (class size budget: FlatStore
   was at 1167 LOC vs 1148 baseline).
7. src/back/core/graphdb/lakebase/_companion_rebuild.py (new): one function
   rebuilding the certified and asserted companions in the same transactions
   as before, plus the asserted set.
8. src/back/core/graphdb/interfaces/SearchCacheMixin.py: inventory keys
   `adj_out_asserted`, `adj_in_asserted`, `props_asserted`.
9. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/BuildObjects.py: `_asserted_*` suffixes
   classified as search cache and stripped to the graph base (Lakebase grouping).
10. src/front/static/config/js/settings.js: same suffixes in the Lakebase
    grouping; comment updated.
11. src/front/static/query/js/query-build-cache.js and query-sync.js: three new
    cache rows (Adjacency out/in and Properties, asserted).
12. docs/backend.md, README.md: companion tables and the rebuild paragraph.
13. Tests: tests/units/graphdb/test_asserted_companions.py (new, 9 tests:
    relation detection, routing with and without domain, asserted entity-search
    probe, rebuild builds asserted companions from the asserted view, grouping,
    expansion SQL for the Original Graph); tests/units/graphdb/test_lakebase_adjacency.py
    (3 new tests; rebuild transaction order now ends with the asserted props);
    tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_delta_flat_store.py (expansion tests now use
    the `_graph` relation for the certified cache; 8 companion jobs).

Upgrade note:
Graphs built before this change have no `_asserted_*` companions. Their Original
Graph reads take the SPO path (no cache) until the next Build or Refresh cache.
With the search cache forced on (`force_on`), Original Graph reads raise the
cache-missing error until then.

Not done (follow-up): the MCP tool description and agent prompts still say
"live graph" (AI feature gate, see the previous section).

