================================================================================
Tests: validate the search cache of both graphs (Certified and Original)
================================================================================

Context:
The previous section added the asserted companions and was covered by SQL-shape
tests. This one runs the stores' real cache rebuild and read SQL against the
in-memory SQLite doubles, on Delta and Lakebase, and checks the behaviour of
both caches on one scenario (mapped data, a derived edge and a derived-only
entity, a user-added edge, a user-deleted edge).

Changes:
1. tests/units/graphdb/test_search_cache_both_graphs.py (new, 54 test runs:
   every scenario runs on Delta and Lakebase, some also once per graph):
   - companion contents: the Certified adjacency / props / entity search hold
     the derived edge and the derived entity, the Original ones do not; a
     user-deleted edge is in neither; the two families use different tables;
   - reads served from the cache: expansion, neighbours, entities by type,
     Preview seeds and the property payload return the right graph for each;
   - parity: every cache-aware read gives the same answer with the cache
     (auto) and without it (force_off), for each graph, plus a guard that the
     two runs really take different paths;
   - no cache / old graph: before the first build, and for a graph that only
     has the certified family, reads fall back to SPO and stay correct;
   - snapshot and refresh: an edit reaches the cache only at the next rebuild;
     a refresh never moves a derived triple into the Original Graph; a full
     rebuild drops derived rows from the Certified cache only; a user deletion
     leaves both caches at the next refresh.
2. tests/fixtures/sqlite_graph_backends.py: the doubles now run the cache
   rebuild. Spark: `CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE ... USING DELTA [CLUSTER BY] AS`,
   `DROP VIEW IF EXISTS` on a table (no-op), simple `LEFT ANTI JOIN <cte> ON`,
   and a lock + `check_same_thread=False` (the rebuild runs one CTAS per
